{0 console-eio}

Progress rows for OCaml command-line tools, run with
{{:https://github.com/ocaml-multicore/eio}Eio}.

[console-eio] runs a {!Console.Display} on the terminal. It finds whether
the output is a terminal and its size, redraws the progress rows, gives the
program's output and its [Logs] messages to the task current where they are
printed, under its row, or prints them above the rows outside a task, and
gives the terminal back however the program ends. On a pipe or in a CI log
it prints plain lines instead. The smallest program:

{@ocaml[
let build display =
  Console.Display.with_task display "compile" (fun step ->
      Console.Display.set_count step ~cur:1 ~total:2;
      Console.Display.log step "ocamlopt parser.ml";
      Console.Display.set_count step ~cur:2 ~total:2)

let main () =
  Eio_main.run @@ fun env ->
  Console_eio.run ~clock:(Eio.Stdenv.mono_clock env) ~header:"Building" build
]}

{!page-tutorial} builds a whole command step by step: options for colour and
theme, a table, progress rows and a test of its output.

{1:modules Modules}

{ul
{- {!Console_eio}: runs a display and decides on colour for the outputs the
   program left alone.}
{- {!Console_eio.Prompt}: questions asked on the terminal, a line, a yes or
   no, or a password.}}

The widgets, the themes and the rules of the display are in the [console]
package: {!Console}.
